343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 160 0 R
/T (% Assemble KKT system A = [0, y_tr'; y_tr, Omega+\(1/gamma\)*eye\(n\)]; rhs = [0; ones\(n,1\)]; sol = A \\ rhs; b_val = sol\(1\);  alpha = sol\(2:end\);)
/E (% Assemble KKT system A = [0, y_tr'; y_tr, Omega+\(1/gamma\)*eye\(n\)]; rhs = [0; ones\(n,1\)]; sol = A \\ rhs; b_val = sol\(1\);  alpha = sol\(2:end\);)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 160 0 R
/T (% Classify test points for k = 1:n_test   Ktest = arrayfun\(@\(i\)K\(Xtr\(i,:\),Xte\(k,:\)\),1:n\)';   pred\(k\) = sign\(alpha'*\(y_tr.*Ktest\)+b_val\); end acc = mean\(pred == y_te\);)
/E (% Classify test points for k = 1:n_test   Ktest = arrayfun\(@\(i\)K\(Xtr\(i,:\),Xte\(k,:\)\),1:n\)';   pred\(k\) = sign\(alpha'*\(y_tr.*Ktest\)+b_val\); end acc = mean\(pred == y_te\);)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 160 0 R
/T (To make the implementation more reliable, we did not choose gamma and sigma arbitrarily. We used a small validation split inside the training data and selected the hyperparameters that maximized validation accuracy. After selecting the best pair, we retrained the LS-SVM on the whole training-validation set and evaluated it only once on the independent test set, in order to obtain an unbiased final performance estimate.)
/E (To make the implementation more reliable, we did not choose gamma and sigma arbitrarily. We used a small validation split inside the training data and selected the hyperparameters that maximized validation accuracy. After selecting the best pair, we retrained the LS-SVM on the whole training-validation set and evaluated it only once on the independent test set, in order to obtain an unbiased final performance estimate.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [18]
>>
